---
/**
 * t68 · Falloff
 *
 * Hozz's lens spends its whole tone budget on the outer band and leaves the
 * middle plain. This is that method applied to a speech bubble.
 *
 * Every tone is a level line of the silhouette: distance measured inward from
 * the edge, brightest one pixel in, falling continuously to a deep core. The
 * important part is that the distance is measured across body *and* tail
 * together, so the bands wrap the tail exactly as they wrap the shoulders and
 * the tail stops being an appendage. A tail that is shaded by a separate rule
 * always looks glued on; this one cannot.
 *
 * Contour alone is even, and even is inert, so the band strength is biased
 * along a top-left to bottom-right axis. The rim is brightest at the upper
 * shoulder and has dimmed to almost nothing by the tip of the tail — the mark
 * of a source that is somewhere, not everywhere, which is what makes a still
 * image feel like a moment in a moving one.
 *
 * The carrier is a plain rounded bubble with a longer stepped tail. The face
 * is the family's md/compact/gap-2, sitting on a flat plateau so the falloff
 * never cuts through it.
 *
 * 11 violet tones, indigo core to pale lilac rim.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Falloff">
